LibTomCrypt vendored subset
===========================

Upstream:  https://github.com/libtom/libtomcrypt
Branch:    develop
Commit:    223ecd23b8e8be3f56590d79b259479a9d1c9e52
Date:      2026-08-04
Version:   1.18.2-develop (SCRYPT in headers/tomcrypt.h)

This directory contains an unmodified subset of the upstream tree.  Do not
patch files here -- the whole point of keeping them pristine is that the
subset can be refreshed with a plain file copy.  Configuration lives in
crypto/accel_ltc_config.h, which crypto/CMakeLists.txt force-includes into
every vendored file, never in headers/tomcrypt_custom.h.

The previous vendored copy (removed in c912d090, Sep 2025) was LibTomCrypt
1.17 from 2011 and had been hand-edited, which is why it was never updated.

Layout
------
  headers/   verbatim copy of upstream src/headers/
  src/       flattened copy of the algorithm files listed below

File set
--------
  hashes:        md4.c md5.c sha1.c sha1_desc.c sha256.c sha256_desc.c
  hash helper:   hash_memory.c            (needed by hmac_init for long keys)
  ciphers:       des.c
  mac:           hmac_init.c hmac_process.c hmac_done.c hmac_memory.c
  misc:          zeromem.c burn_stack.c mem_neq.c copy_or_zeromem.c
  registry:      crypt_hash_descriptor.c crypt_register_hash.c
                 crypt_find_hash.c crypt_hash_is_valid.c

SHA-256 is not used by any PPP/RADIUS primitive; it is required by the SSTP
Compound MAC (MS-SSTP 3.3.5.2.3) when the certificate hash protocol is
SHA-256.

Deliberately not vendored, though the algorithms above reference them
upstream -- our configuration compiles all three to nothing:

  sha1_x86.c, sha256_x86.c   SHA-NI/AVX2 paths, excluded by LTC_NO_ASM
  crypt_argchk.c             crypt_argchk(), unreferenced at ARGTYPE 4

That makes the file set depend on crypto/accel_ltc_config.h: dropping
LTC_NO_ASM or lowering ARGTYPE means copying those files back in, otherwise
the build fails on an undefined symbol rather than silently misbehaving.

Refreshing
----------
  git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/libtom/libtomcrypt ltc
  cp ltc/src/headers/*.h crypto/libtomcrypt/headers/
  cp ltc/src/hashes/{md4,md5,sha1,sha1_desc}.c \
     ltc/src/hashes/sha2/{sha256,sha256_desc}.c \
     ltc/src/hashes/helper/hash_memory.c \
     ltc/src/ciphers/des.c \
     ltc/src/mac/hmac/{hmac_init,hmac_process,hmac_done,hmac_memory}.c \
     ltc/src/misc/{zeromem,burn_stack,mem_neq,copy_or_zeromem}.c \
     ltc/src/misc/crypt/{crypt_hash_descriptor,crypt_register_hash,crypt_find_hash,crypt_hash_is_valid}.c \
     crypto/libtomcrypt/src/
  then update the commit id above and run the known-answer tests:

     cmake -S . -B build -DCRYPTO=INTERNAL
     make -C build accel-crypto-test && ./build/crypto/accel-crypto-test

Known upstream issue
--------------------
headers/tomcrypt_custom.h lines 764 and 768 have a stray ')' terminating the
#if expressions inside the "#if !defined(LTC_ECB_MODE)" guard:

    #if defined(LTC_CFB_MODE) || ... || defined(LTC_XTS_MODE) )

This is a preprocessor syntax error that only becomes reachable in a minimal
build that leaves LTC_ECB_MODE undefined, which is why upstream has not hit
it.  We define LTC_ECB_MODE, which skips the whole guarded block; that flag
is also required for the symmetric_ECB declarations in tomcrypt_private.h.
Reported upstream -- once fixed, LTC_ECB_MODE can stay anyway (it costs
nothing, as none of the mode .c files are compiled in).
